From 104b32ae1ae9f9d6f81cc5d76807e51093a5213f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:51:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] preserve rejected retain custody without disabling
 failure enforcement

Why: first-wins retain custody was used as observer suppression even after a definitive Board rejection, so a live worker escaped max-runtime and a dead worker waited for lease expiry. Separate immutable custody from observer-held state; atomically reserve one ordinary fallback release under the rejected command, preserve its bytes, and keep pending/unknown/ACK/confirmed commands held. ACK and settled replies are monotone; transient transport refusals remain recoverable; canonical confirmation uses a custody CAS. Close the primary Hub on all errors and register retain in the metrics schema.

Proof: metrics and actual timeout/crash/failed-result regressions reproduced RED on prior head in b1-rejection-red.log. ACK/transient and confirmation-race cases reproduced RED before their corrections. Final shared retain/failure/updater/observer tests pass via scripts/run_tests.sh; real failed-child result writer and unmocked observer included. No original incident release, new authority or B2 changes.
